:: Carter Bedroom Play Evidence [nobr]

/* Intro */
<<set $Minutes += 20>>
You and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> decide to play a game of, surprise surprise, superheroes; at the start of which <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> produces two capes for you both to wear. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Well, we have to look the part!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> explains as you give him a smirk, <span style="color:Pink">finding his childish demeaner cute.</span> <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Alright, here’s the case! The local jewelry store is being robbed, we gotta go in and stop them! Are you ready, sidekick!”</span> You decide not to argue with you being the sidekick and instead just follow <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s lead. <br>

    <<set _ad to [
        {
            Name: "Carter",
            State: {
                Outfit: "Everyday",
                Mouth: "Happy",
            },	
        },
        {
            Name: "Player",
            State: {
                Mouth: "Happy",
            },	
        },
    ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

The two of you bust into the jewelry store that looks suspiciously like <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s bedroom and begin battle with the stuffed enemies of justice. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s collection of stuffed animals is pretty impressive, and you guess by how beat up they are and the fact that they are stored in his closet that their sole purpose is as enemies for him to fight rather than a source of comfort, like they are with Noah, so you don’t hold back as you and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> spin and slam them about! <br>
<br>
<span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“I questioned the ones who are still conscious.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> says after the battle comes to an end, deepening his voice as much as he can, <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“It seems the leader got away with the goods. I’ll keep questioning them, you see if you can find any evidence of who did this.”</span> You nod, beginning to look around the room to see if you can find what devious stuffed villain is behind this. <br>
<br>
Though there isn’t much in terms of evidence to be found, considering this is all a game, but you figure that a pretend robbery would need some pretend evidence, so you look around the room to see what you can find. You spot a toy dart gun in the corner, thinking about how this could maybe have been left behind by the big boss and may have his finger prints. <span style="color:Yellow">That would work… then again, as you spy <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s dirty laundry basket in his closet, you get another possible idea.</span> <br>
<br>

<div id="choice">
    <<link "Plant the gun<br>">>
    <<replace "#choice">>
        You reach over and grab the toy gun, placing it, along with some other unrelated things, in a pile slightly under the bed. You then pretend to discover it, gasping and calling <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> over. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“What did you find?”</span> He asks, sounding serious. You hold out the gun and he nods, <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“I see, that does narrow it down. This weapon is made by the Carmine Foundation, a group known for black market weapons. They keep a log of every gun sold, though they aren’t known to give up their customers.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> thinks for a long moment, either for dramatic effect or to try and come up with a possible solution. <br>
        <br>
        <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“I think I may know someone who can hack into their system, at least get us some info. Good work, sidekick!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> gives you a smile and a thumbs up. The two of you finish off here, putting some of his stuffed animals in cute plastic handcuffs and handing them off to the police to be put back in jail, aka <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s closet, before heading to go and find <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s ally. <br>
        <br>
        The game goes on for a long while, with many twists and turns in the story and lots of action and detective work. <span style="color:LightGreen">Overall, it is a pretty fun time and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> sure seems to know how to weave together an interesting superhero story. Probably from all the comics he’s read.</span> <br>
        
        <span style="color:Green">+Carter Fun</span><br>
        <<set $HangOutNeed.Fun += 10>>
        <span style="color:green">+Carter Comfort</span><br>
        <<set $HangOutNeed.Comfort += 5>>
        <<needChange "Fun" 10>>
        <<socialChange "Carter" 1>>
        <br>
        [[Continue|Carter House Carter Bedroom]]

    <</replace>>
    <</link>>
    <<link "Plant some of Carter’s dirty underwear<br>">>
    <<replace "#choice">>
        <span style="color:Pink">With a devious grin you reach into <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s basket and pull out a pair of underwear, ensuring you get one from the top. It’s still warm on the crotch area and you wager <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> much have only changed out of these earlier today. You give it a quick look over as you move it about in your hand, smirking at how small it looks loose like this, before placing it under the bed just barely in view.</span> You then pretend to discover it, gasping as you call <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> over. <br>
        <br>
        <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“What did you find?”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> asks, keeping up the serious tone in his voice. You point to the tiny splash of color poking out from the bed and he nods, though give it a look of confusion, as if he’s trying to figure out what it is. You reach down and pretend to struggle to get it before suddenly pulling it out and holding it up. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“What is- Ahhh! H- hey!”</span> <span style="color:Pink"><span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s voice goes from his attempt at a deep to even more high-pitched than usual as he tries to snatch it away from you. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“T- that’s not the villains! Give it!”</span> <br>

            <<set _ad to [
                {
                    Name: "Carter",
                    State: {
                        Outfit: "Everyday",
                        Mouth: "Frown",
                        Eyes: "Mad",
                        Blush: 1,
                    },	
                },
                {
                    Name: "Player",
                    State: {
                        Mouth: "Smirk",
                        Eyes: "Tired",
                    },	
                },
            ]>>
            <<ad _ad>>

        You laugh, holding the underwear just out of reach as you playfully inspect it, making comments on the villain as you do. Such as you’d guess the villain was a very small boy, based on the size, or how they must not shake off their wiener enough when they pee, since there is a slight wet stain on the crotch area. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> becomes more and more flustered as you go, desperately trying to grab it from you until you both tumble to the ground and he finally gets it away from you.</span> <br>
        <br>
        <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“You’re the real villain!”</span> He says as he shoves the dirty underwear down far into the basket. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Traitor…”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> pouts for a minute, though you eventually get him laughing as you make up some ridiculous villain idea about some underwear snatcher who steals underwear to frame people for his crimes. <span style="color:Pink"><span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> finds it so amusing that the story eventually has you both confront the mastermind, though he doesn’t let you use anymore of his underwear as props.</span> <br>

        <span style="color:Green">+Carter Fun</span><br>
